Since this manuscript was first submitted, observations by Mooley et al. (2018) have been published indicating that the source was unresolved at 230 days. The FWHM values we reported in Section 3 are consistent with this measurement. However we also found that the choked jet model generally predicts a larger image than the successful jet. We predict that if VLBI observations were obtained at \\sim 400 days, they would be marginally resolved for either model. A larger FWHM value of 7 mas favors a choked jet while a smaller value of 4.5 mas favors a successful jet.

